{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras","id":494739,"title":"Beast Dark Eras?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-28T07:06:45-07:00","id":494739,"title":"Beast Dark Eras?","content":"So, in the comments to this week's <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/we-started-like-you-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Monday Meeting</a>, someone asked about getting a Beast Dark Era as a stretch goal, and Matt asked if they had an era in mind.<br /> <br /> I suggested:<br /> <br /> 1950s USA/USSR - the Cold War, fear of sympathisers, fear of nuclear annihilation.<br /> <br /> 1890s Japan, around the time Lafcaido Hearn started collecting youkai stories (adding another Japanese era, exploring Beasts' history in Japan and how they played into youkai stories).<br /> <br /> C.1100-800 BCE Greece, aka the Greek Dark Ages, after the end of the Bronze Age, the years before classical Greece gets up and going.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Any other era ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:11:07-07:00","id":494754,"title":"","content":"Book of Invasions Ireland! Beastly Fomorians versus the God-Heroes, The Tuatha De Danaan!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:32:33-07:00","id":494778,"title":"","content":"1890s Japan and Lafcadio Hearn please. PLEASE. My fondness for youkai mythos and &quot;Gensokyo in NWoD&quot; scratch need to be sated.<br /> <br /> Greek Dark Ages would be fantastic for some of the mythological flavor though. But Book Of Invasions or Ulster Cycle Ireland sound like they could be amazing in tone and inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:51:09-07:00","id":494791,"title":"","content":"THey could, couldn't they?<br /> <br /> And get this-Book of Invasions(at least) is almost certainly Neolithic(don't have my notes on the vague guessery at this time), so that entire thing about monsters going back to one root? Certainly could be played with there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:13:44-07:00","id":494838,"title":"","content":"Veeeery interesting grounds to explore that setting, indeed.<br /> <br /> Also I'm caught up in imagining Scathach as a Beast with the Fortress Of Shadows as her Lair, with Cu Chullain as a student who later became a Hero. Or maybe a Beast himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:13:50-07:00","id":494839,"title":"","content":"Besides Beast Dark Eras, I would like a kind of appendix with Beast siderbars for the eras presented in the Dark Eras corebook and Companion like the other splats are getting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:15:11-07:00","id":494843,"title":"","content":"That might be too much to hope for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:06:38-07:00","id":494890,"title":"","content":"Given that Beast is getting constructed specifically with crossovers in mind, it might be doable to just have Beast sidebars spread throughout the other Eras. &quot;This is how you could patch Beasts into this one&quot;, &quot;These are some things people were super scared of at this point; think Beasts&quot;<br /> <br /> Caveat: I haven't read any of the Dark Eras previews yet, so I don't know what the tone or flow of the writing is. From my complete outsider's perspective, though, this seems like it could be workable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:07:02-07:00","id":494891,"title":"","content":"Actually, it may be easier in some respects than a whole chapter. Dave explained in the Mage forums that those sidebars have at most a paragraph or two about what is happening in other lines at that time. So it wouldn't be too hard to throw a paragraph in on Beasts, especially since the book is still being thrown together.<br /> <br /> Writing a whole new chapter would likely mean getting members from the Beast team to step aside and write it (to make sure it stays on point thematically and any new mechanics for the era fit), rather than just have the writers of each of the Dark Age chapter just throw in a general blurb with Matt's approval. <br /> <br /> That said... I would love Ireland. I vote for the Ulster Cycle of Irish Mythos rather than the Mythological Cycle. Don't get me wrong, I love the Tuatha and Fomorian conflict, but I feel that it is too mystical almost, dealing with gods and monsters, rather then men (it would work better in a Changeling or Mage game in my mind). The Ulster Cycle focuses on men interacting with the world of monsters, being more akin to the monster Mythos of Greece.<br /> <br /> That, and the Ulster cycle has C\u00fa Chulainn, whom I think would be a great example of a famous beast. Though elements of his story are classically heroic (son of a god, virgin birth, trials and quests) much of his overall story could read as that of a Beast: many of his deeds are borderline psychopathic, such as building walls out of the corpses of an enemy army that he single handedly destroyed or kidnapping a princess and stealing the wealth, he is the great grandson of a Fomorian, Balor (so we know he has a bit of a monsterous heritage).Heck, during said battle, he manages to keep going even when the Rival army's champion is backed by a god (The Morrigan), wounding her everytime she interferes, eventually winning despite her interference. <br /> <br /> And then there is the Riastrad (Warp Spasms), which throws him into an unstoppable rage and transforms him (Atavisms):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first warp-spasm seized C\u00fachulainn, and made him into a monstrous thing, hideous and shapeless, unheard of. His shanks and his joints, every knuckle and angle and organ from head to foot, shook like a tree in the flood or a reed in the stream. His body made a furious twist inside his skin, so that his feet and shins switched to the rear and his heels and calves switched to the front... On his head the temple-sinews stretched to the nape of his neck, each mighty, immense, measureless knob as big as the head of a month-old child... he sucked one eye so deep into his head that a wild crane couldn't probe it onto his cheek out of the depths of his skull; the other eye fell out along his cheek. His mouth weirdly distorted: his cheek peeled back from his jaws until the gullet appeared, his lungs and his liver flapped in his mouth and throat, his lower jaw struck the upper a lion-killing blow, and fiery flakes large as a ram's fleece reached his mouth from his throat... The hair of his head twisted like the tangle of a red thornbush stuck in a gap; if a royal apple tree with all its kingly fruit were shaken above him, scarce an apple would reach the ground but each would be spiked on a bristle of his hair as it stood up on his scalp with rage. </div> </div> </div>Even his death sounds more like how you hunt a monster: three magically forged Spears, wielded by a man seeking vengeance and blessed by a queen who is the mortal enemy of C\u00fa Chulainn... And he keeps fighting after death, cutting off the sword arm of Lugaid (the man who killed him) when Lugaid attempts to behead C\u00fa Chulainn. <br /> <br /> I see him as a great example of an Anakim, with a Hunger for Power or Punishment (lots of his stories are him besting others, including kings, or bringing destruction on those who broke the ancient code). Just an idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 04-28-2015, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:18:45-07:00","id":494928,"title":"","content":"Really, any of the Irish cycles would make for great works, and certainly any after the Mythological Cycle would be easier to pin. Hell, in my inital pitch for the cycles, I did mention the Ulster Cycle as my second one to go to.<br /> <br /> That said, a mixture of experimentality, grand stakes, deconstruction, and just the sheer fact I'm more familiar with it is why I go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:24:59-07:00","id":494932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=494928#post494928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, any of the Irish cycles would make for great works, and certainly any after the Mythological Cycle would be easier to pin. Hell, in my inital pitch for the cycles, I did mention the Ulster Cycle as my second one to go to.<br /> <br /> That said, a mixture of experimentality, grand stakes, deconstruction, and just the sheer fact I'm more familiar with it is why I go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I am in complete agreement: Any Irish cycle would be awesome. I just flip my preferences (ulster&gt;mythology), probably cause I read the Ulster cycle translations in college and only reviewed the Mythology Cycle as background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:38:31-07:00","id":494945,"title":"","content":"I did the <i>exact</i> opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:48:44-07:00","id":494958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=494843#post494843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be too much to hope for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually since it seen will be a paragraph for each splat per Era it will probably be much easier than a full Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:51:53-07:00","id":494964,"title":"","content":"It might be easier, but it's still unlikely, given the design parameters for Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:19:40-07:00","id":495046,"title":"","content":"Maybe a little PDF add on afterwards. Similar to what happened with Mirrors? That way, it doesn't throw off the count and could allow for the addition of the blurbs by era as well as a new chapter unique to Beast. Then again, that could be pushing it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=494945#post494945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did the <i>exact</i> opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! I really wish I could have spent more time studying the Irish Mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T14:01:09-07:00","id":495165,"title":"","content":"I'm big on the 1890s Japan era idea.<br /> <br /> I'm also suggesting a post-Babylonian/Hammurabi Empire Mesopotamian setting. The first recorded laws have been put into place, and civilization is in retreat with the death of the archetypal Lawgiver. Now is the age of monsters beyond the safety of the walls... and going unnoticed within them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:23:47-07:00","id":495285,"title":"","content":"<i>You're off the edge of the map there matey! And here be monsters!!!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:01:23-07:00","id":495498,"title":"","content":"I don't know how many we can fit in since there probably will be other stretch goals like fiction(a must) and things like a Ready-Made Characters or a city guide, but since Beast is perfect for crossovers I think we should push for some joint Eras.<br /> Suggestions:<br /> <br /> Beast and Hunter: Book of Judges-&gt; What if some of the Judges were actually Heroes(Samson comes to mind) as well with some Hunter in the mix?<br /> Beast and Geist: Golden Age of Piracy-&gt; The Makara having fun<br /> Beast and Vampire-&gt; Chicago World Fair<br /> Ps: Yes I am shameless suggesting some Dark Eras runner ups, but I actually think those Eras would work well with Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:13:48-07:00","id":495524,"title":"","content":"I had suggested the Trail of Tears as a crossover between Beast and Geist in the comments section of the Monday Meeting notes, as well as the possibility of a classical Greece setting as a standalone or as a crossover with Changeling or Hunter.<br /> <br /> After giving it some thought, I think that the Dancing Plague of 1518. It is something utterly bizarre that could easily be attributed to supernatural forces in the World of Darkness. The uncontrollable dancing could even be used to create a new Nightmare. Maybe it could be something like this:<br /> <br /> YOUR BODY IS NOT YOUR OWN<br /> <br /> Why are you doing this? You never intended to start, and now, you can't even stop. Your body dances like a marionette at the end of its strings, while you stare helplessly out of your eyes.<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Satiety vs. Composure + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> Normal: The victim gains the Dominated condition (see Vampire: The Requiem 2nd edition), finding themselves unable to stop going through the physical motions of whatever action the Beast has commanded. The victim may run, fight, or dance without cease for the remainder of the scene, depending on what the Beast desires.<br /> <br /> High Satiety: The Beast gains more control over the actions that the victim can take. For instance, the Beast may choose a specific target for the victim to attack or the type of dance that must be performed.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The Beast may spend multiple Satiety on this effect, causing it to become contagious. Anybody in close proximity or interacting with the victim must roll Resolve + Composure or begin to suffer the effects as though they had been the original target. Each Satiety spent passes the contagious nature of the effect on to further victims. At one Satiety, only those interacting with the original victim will need to resist, while for two Satiety the ones infected by the first victim will also be contagious. The Beast is immune to this effect, but the Beast's allies are not.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The effects of the Nightmare will linger indefinitely. The victim will continue to perform the actions even after the scene has concluded. The only way to break them of the effect is to forcibly prevent them from being able to perform the activity for a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:33:03-07:00","id":496194,"title":"","content":"Also, a Beast/Innocents crossover in the Blitz would be nice. What if Peter Pan was actually a Beast and Neverland it's Lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 04-29-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:17:11-07:00","id":496247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=496194#post496194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a Beast/Innocents crossover in the Blitz would be nice. What if Peter Pan was actually a Beast and Neverland it's Lairs?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would give Neverland a decidedly darker tone. I'm reminded of the sample in the &quot;Families&quot; where &quot;He'd never hurt one of his kids...until one of them crosses the line. And then he ain't one his kids anymore..&quot; or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:26:53-07:00","id":496249,"title":"","content":"I'd personally love to see some pre-Columbian America. I mean, chances are no one would write it, but I'd love it all the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T08:42:45-07:00","id":496332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=496247#post496247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would give Neverland a decidedly darker tone. I'm reminded of the sample in the &quot;Families&quot; where &quot;He'd never hurt one of his kids...until one of them crosses the line. And then he ain't one his kids anymore..&quot; or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not far off the original to be honest. And I don't mind deconstructive readings, I mean things like the implication that Peter kills Lost Boys who grow up too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vedic India strikes me as a good era for Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:27:35-07:00","id":496940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=496332#post496332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vedic India strikes me as a good era for Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe as a crossover Era with Changeling?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:49:16-07:00","id":496951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=496194#post496194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a Beast/Innocents crossover in the Blitz would be nice. What if Peter Pan was actually a Beast and Neverland it's Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>About <b>London Blitz Era</b>: I would point out this combination is golden, as you can be loneley child thrown in alien enviorment, monster under it's bed or just that thing that watch out from the window both of them to sate it's Hunger, in the times of great terror on the world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The victim of fear ( child), the source of fear ( supernaturals/monsters? Beasts? ), the guardian of this fear ( the other Begotten ) or even to play the fear of eveyone of those groups in times of war. What even more disturbing Homecoming to have is that your repeating child nightmares are <b>your very own Beast Soul</b>?<br /> <br /> And even then random vampire that raised from grave on battlefield, totally lost in their undead condition. Or werewolf that slaughter battalion pressed to anger, and now left without guidence. The both literal children and metaphorical Children need to take care of them or confront them.<br /> <br /> Looks I finally got idea for mine first chronicle in Beast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Really, I need this setting right now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-29-2015, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:09:44-07:00","id":497022,"title":"","content":"Another possibility could be ancient Sumer. I'm thinking in the Gigamesh Poem, the story of Gigamesh and Enkidu, it could be the tale of a Hero (Gigamesh) against a Beast (Enkidu), which at the end, became allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:58:12-07:00","id":497044,"title":"","content":"Yes, absolutely Babylon! Many of the family names stem from the cradle of civilization I'm willing to bet it'll be covered in he corebook. Gilgamesh and Enkidu aside, I personally like how it's humanity's first major attempt to shield themselves from the primordial nightmares... and I doubt the Five Families were too keen on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:23:31-07:00","id":497098,"title":"","content":"Contemporary to Ruins of Empire, turn of the century Himalayas and Mongolia, during the reign of the 13th Dalai Lama, as British Adventurism, Russian expansionism, and decaying Chinese power fall in from all sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T05:24:11-07:00","id":497337,"title":"","content":"Hm, I'd throw in the Great White North during the indians and furriers days- Amerindian monsters, european monsters, are beasts responsible for the wendigo myth, or is there something else stalking the harsh winter nights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T06:07:17-07:00","id":527579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras#post494739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the comments to this week's <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/we-started-like-you-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Monday Meeting</a>, someone asked about getting a Beast Dark Era as a stretch goal, and Matt asked if they had an era in mind.<br /> <br /> I suggested:<br /> <br /> 1950s USA/USSR - the Cold War, fear of sympathisers, fear of nuclear annihilation.<br /> Thoughts? Any other era ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like...the true story of Godzilla to me.<br /> <br /> Hm...reminded of the 70s movie &quot;Jaws&quot; the movie molded the fear of the ocean and beaches pretty well with it's predecessor &quot;Creature from the Black Lagoon.&quot;<br /> Hmf...I suppose one can garner a lot of inspiration from those old horror movies.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:18:51-07:00","id":527959,"title":"","content":"Bacon Rebellion-Era West Virginia. A story emphasizing the Begotten as fixers and traffickers in Colonial Virginia, particularly among disaffected factions within the Cryptopoli of early America.<br /> <br /> Alexandrian Middle East. A story about the Helenization of the near east, and what <i>really</i> stopped Alexander of Macedon from conquering India.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:33:06-07:00","id":540200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast The Primordial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we pass <b>$80,000</b> of contributions, we will create a <b>Beast</b>-themed historical chapter for the <b>nWoD Dark Eras Companion</b>. A PDF of this chapter will be sent to every backer who pledged for a Reward Tier that includes a PDF of <b>Beast: The Primordial</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it'll end up in amongst these...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RichT here with the confirmed list of the Dark Eras for the <b>nWoD Dark Eras Companion</b> stretch goal project. Just got these from Black Hat Matt McFarland, and in no particular order:<ul><li>Second Sight: Age of Spiritualism</li> <li>Demon: Russian Revolution</li> <li>Mummy: Cleopatran Egypt</li> <li>Promethean: Year Without a Summer</li> <li>Geist: Roanoke</li> <li>Werewolf: Forsaken by Rome</li> <li>Mage: Mutapan Empire (backer resurrected era)</li> <li>Promethean: Black Death (backer resurrected era)</li> <li>Promethean: 30 Years War (backer suggested era)</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:13:43-07:00","id":540531,"title":"","content":"I think you only get the Beast chapter, though. Unless you've backed the Dark Eras book.<br /> <br /> Lets have something out there. How about the early 1900s Antarctic expeditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:34:05-07:00","id":540567,"title":"","content":"I didn't know the 30 Year War got confirmed... damn, there goes my big pitch for another Promethean Dark Era in the English Civil War up through the Fire of 1666, in which the last of the previous (pre-Frankenstein) fire-aligned Lineage, the Belenus (Wickermen), go instinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:36:09-07:00","id":540575,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">1) Bring back &quot;Jazz Age Vampire&quot;, double-sized with Beast. The 20s lets us pull on Lovecraft, cast against the racism of the era deconstructing it (it was the height of post-Abolition anti-black violence in the US), which in turn is cast against the Harlem Renaissance. Meanwhile you have all the Prohibition/Swinging 20s/Organized Crime themes that made it appealing for Vampire in the first place.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2) Contemporaneous to &quot;Ruins of Empire&quot;, a separate setting focused on Tibet/Mongolia at the dawn of the 20th Century. Under the shadow of the decaying grasp of Imperial China, Russian Expansionism, and British Adventurism, during the reign of the 13th Dalai Lama. You have the &quot;explorers vs. indigenous&quot; themes to invert the Hero's Journey, without the mass genocide of doing that story in the Americas or Australia. Not to mention the rich supply of Himalayan folklore to draw on (who wouldn't want to play a Yeti?!) Perhaps there was some attempt to create a civilization-scale shared Lair by the Beasts of the Himalayas faced with expanding &quot;Heroic&quot; encroachment?<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">3) Out of respect to Grendel &amp; his Mom, double the wordcount on Viking Werewolf to add Beasts. (doesn't look possible since that's in the Dark Eras core, not the Companion)<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">4) Prehistoric Mesopotamia, to play with the story of Qingu, child of Tiamat vs. Marduk as the father of civilization.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:00:05-07:00","id":540624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=540531#post540531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you only get the Beast chapter, though. Unless you've backed the Dark Eras book.<br /> <br /> Lets have something out there. How about the early 1900s Antarctic expeditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the Mountains of Madness, anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T23:09:40-07:00","id":540661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=540575#post540575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0F2105\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">4) Prehistoric Mesopotamia, to play with the story of Qingu, child of Tiamat vs. Marduk as the father of civilization.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I love it, even if the ancient middle East is getting a tad crowded in nWoD; (FCG's Hunting Grounds: Sumer, Ancient Mysteries Flashpoint: Black Streets of Babylon, Irem, Ki-En-Gir, Ur (&amp; the 'goddess' Inanna from the Deava Clanbook). If we keep it up, we might have to start coming up with...(shudders) <i>answers</i>.<br /> <br /> Still it is an area &amp; era that hasn't been really explored and there is enough 'family' presence to spice up the old Kinship.<br /> Prehistoric Mesopotamia gets my vote. Too bad this isn't a vote.<br /> <br /> Still, it makes me revisit the Poisoned One &amp; her 'profane citadel' as mentioned in the Rotting Temple write up in Book of the Deceived.<br /> <i>...He cast a tribe among the monsters and met them with flame and thunder whenever they tried to leave.</i>..<br /> <i>...One woman of the 11th generation grew to adulthood without madness or a distorted form...<br /> ...He wished to show that he could raise a civilization beyond the Law...</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Hello, Mother&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:02:16-07:00","id":540723,"title":"","content":"I want something really fucking ancient and mythical-feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T00:39:40-07:00","id":540738,"title":"","content":"Something in the Cold War to cross-over with the Unchained, being as they're the weird odd-ones out not related to the Beasts. I'm think the nightmare jungles of Vietnam or Nicaragua myself. Bring on the horror. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:12:07-07:00","id":543978,"title":"","content":"Hey, at what point in history do you think the Beasts made the transition from actual beasts to the Flesh/Astral combos they are now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T10:23:14-07:00","id":543988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=