cents crossover in the Blitz would be nice. What if Peter Pan was actually a Beast and Neverland it's Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>I Would Enjoy that... Narnia.... Is So Much darker if you use this.... Hell or Any of the Storys about the Blitz. I Would love too see it. That and Cold War for me Seem too Work (I don't think it'd need a Full chapter just a Sidebar, but then I wouldn't Argue against a Full Chapter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:17:07-07:00","id":545710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=545703#post545703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I Would Enjoy that... Narnia.... Is So Much darker if you use this.... Hell or Any of the Storys about the Blitz. I Would love too see it. That and Cold War for me Seem too Work (I don't think it'd need a Full chapter just a Sidebar, but then I wouldn't Argue against a Full Chapter).</div> </div> </div> </div>David Hasslehoff is a Ravager who fed on the destruction of the Berlin Wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:55:49-07:00","id":545745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=545603#post545603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the dark era is in. Im hoping for the crusades</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love a Crusades setting myself, more particularly a 1st Crusade setting... Though not sure if it would work well with Beast as the central splat around it. I'd love to see how Changeling Freeholds based in the Middle East are like, especially dealing with outsiders from their Freehold and from Western Europe coming over. Privateers being a thing and all. The amount of death going through both sides also makes a fairly interesting way to involve Sin-Eaters, the lack of resources making some of the Crusaders allegedly turn to cannibalism makes for some other strong links to the other supernaturals though, Vampires and Uratha being main links, though Beasts could show up in the fearful tales of the 1st Crusade and what men did to each other in this time, sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:58:31-07:00","id":545823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=496194#post496194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a Beast/Innocents crossover in the Blitz would be nice. What if Peter Pan was actually a Beast and Neverland it's Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure CtL has dibs on Pan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:09:58-07:00","id":545843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=545665#post545665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks to the Neolithic Mage/Werewolf setting, we can comfortably say closer to 6-7 thousand years ago, since the Vinca civilization of 5500 bce is pre-Sundering.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the Sundering, is this the name for the event that led to the split from the Supernal and the Gauntlet springing up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:23:32-07:00","id":545860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=545843#post545843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the Sundering, is this the name for the event that led to the split from the Supernal and the Gauntlet springing up?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, only the Gauntlet. The Supernal has always been divorced from reality.<br /> <br /> Well, as much as a source code can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:57:12-07:00","id":545915,"title":"","content":"I meant more the collapse of the Celestial Ladder and the allowance of Abyss to split the pair... Is that still going to be a thing in Mage 2nd edition? I've not been on the Mage boards as it's one of the one lines I don't own, so I know next to nothing on it and don't think I'd be much use in the open dev.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:19:50-07:00","id":545950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=545915#post545915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant more the collapse of the Celestial Ladder and the allowance of Abyss to split the pair... Is that still going to be a thing in Mage 2nd edition? I've not been on the Mage boards as it's one of the one lines I don't own, so I know next to nothing on it and don't think I'd be much use in the open dev.</div> </div> </div> </div>Near as I can tell, the Celestial Ladder fiasco caused Atlantic to be utterly erased from time, zip zoom, never happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:34:49-07:00","id":546003,"title":"","content":"Someone who's probably more familiar with the time period than me has probably already mentioned this, but Viking Beasts would be great. The Vikings loved them some monsters, after all, and there were a massive amount of Giants in their mythos. And giant world eating wolves. Especially the giant wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:00:27-07:00","id":546100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=545843#post545843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the Sundering, is this the name for the event that led to the split from the Supernal and the Gauntlet springing up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, the Sundering is the event of the Gauntlet springing up. It does not refer to the Fall/erasure of a theoretical Atlantis from the timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:03:49-07:00","id":546106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=545915#post545915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant more the collapse of the Celestial Ladder and the allowance of Abyss to split the pair... Is that still going to be a thing in Mage 2nd edition? I've not been on the Mage boards as it's one of the one lines I don't own, so I know next to nothing on it and don't think I'd be much use in the open dev.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Atlantis&quot; is the Diamond's agreed shorthand for &quot;the symbolic perfect city of the Awakened in the Time Before,&quot; and was erased from the timeline in the Fall. No matter how far back you go in time, Atlantis is still &quot;a long time ago&quot;, and sometimes &quot;in the future&quot; and &quot;sideways in time&quot;.<br /> <br /> The second Mage Dark Era is 5500 BC in the Neolithic Balkans, which is before the Sundering, so there's a third world between the Shadow and material instead of a Gauntlet, inhabited by Werewolves and... Things... That don't exist in the modern setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:21:07-07:00","id":546140,"title":"","content":"Last children of Pangaea. I'm really surprised and pleased at how much I'm looking forward to the Neolithic era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:28:44-07:00","id":546148,"title":"","content":"Cool, thank you for the chip in there Dave. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Back on-topic, how about for Beast a setting placed around the era of Homer, the semi-mythical writer in his own right that did the writing of the Odyssey and Iliad (around 900 BCE)? The tales generally fit in with the timeline of The Mighty Despair from Sothis Ascends that some Mummies may still be about and lots of cool Trojan War references can link with lots of other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:29:39-07:00","id":546149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=546106#post546106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Atlantis&quot; is the Diamond's agreed shorthand for &quot;the symbolic perfect city of the Awakened in the Time Before,&quot; and was erased from the timeline in the Fall. No matter how far back you go in time, Atlantis is still &quot;a long time ago&quot;, and sometimes &quot;in the future&quot; and &quot;sideways in time&quot;.<br /> <br /> The second Mage Dark Era is 5500 BC in the Neolithic Balkans, which is before the Sundering, so there's a third world between the Shadow and material instead of a Gauntlet, inhabited by Werewolves and... Things... That don't exist in the modern setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and now, as someone who was kind of 'meh' about the Mage Neolithic Era and voted against it I am so glad we are getting it.<br /> If I had known it was going to be pre-Sundering I would not only have voted for it, but done a merry jig when it won. Seriously, I would have googled how to do a jig then practiced until I did a merry one!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:36:37-07:00","id":546153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=546148#post546148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, thank you for the chip in there Dave. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Back on-topic, how about for Beast a setting placed around the era of Homer, the semi-mythical writer in his own right that did the writing of the Odyssey and Iliad (around 900 BCE)? The tales generally fit in with the timeline of The Mighty Despair from Sothis Ascends that some Mummies may still be about and lots of cool Trojan War references can link with lots of other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to think outside the box, but that would be a classic period to do, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T22:52:53-07:00","id":546550,"title":"","content":"I originally thought of the aridification across the Northern African regions, around 2200-2100BCE. This led to draughts that helped with the collapse of the Old Kingdom of Egypt and also the Akkadian Empire in Mesopotamia (linking to Mummy and Werewolf). I thought this age and setting as it's fairly early in mankind's written history and the kind of fear generated from the period would be something to spawn Beasts, as a shortage of water and thus crops would cause some issues, to say the least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:03:44-07:00","id":546558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=546550#post546550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I originally thought of the aridification across the Northern African regions, around 2200-2100BCE. This led to draughts that helped with the collapse of the Old Kingdom of Egypt and also the Akkadian Empire in Mesopotamia (linking to Mummy and Werewolf). I thought this age and setting as it's fairly early in mankind's written history and the kind of fear generated from the period would be something to spawn Beasts, as a shortage of water and thus crops would cause some issues, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would definitely a good era as well! I keep advocating for the Zanzibar Sultanate in the late 1800s, since there is Omani culture meeting Swahili culture, with the Brits and Germans fighting over the mainland, so I see a lot of potential for Beasts of different nations to meet one another. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:49:36-07:00","id":546597,"title":"","content":"How about Beasts at the time of the Ramayana? I could totally see Beasts as Rakshasas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:49:49-07:00","id":546598,"title":"","content":"Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Pondering on another time of Fear, though it could be a touchy one is the Babylonian's suppression of the Jews, the time of Cyrus the Great of Persia between 586 and 539BCE...<br /> <br /> The Yayoi period of Japan (300 BCE to 300 AD) is something I'd honestly like to see for any line. It was a time of Japanese Shamanism being formed, so there are links to Werewolf, Ulgan Prometheans, Sin-Eaters... It was a practice done for better crops and something I see Beasts tapping into just like the Aridification period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:08:14-07:00","id":560894,"title":"","content":"Considering the whole &quot;using morally questionable terror tactics to force some sense into awful people/societies&quot; thing that Beasts have going for them I can really only think of one point in history that's really fitting.<br /> <br /> Sherman's March (1864 CE, American Civil War).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:16:09-07:00","id":560896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=560894#post560894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the whole &quot;using morally questionable terror tactics to force some sense into awful people/societies&quot; thing that Beasts have going for them I can really only think of one point in history that's really fitting.<br /> <br /> Sherman's March (1864 CE, American Civil War).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, conversely, monsters both Mortal and Beastly running wild during the French Reign of Terror","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:18:43-07:00","id":561038,"title":"","content":"I'll keep asking for a Beast Era set in the Congo Free State (1885 - 1908) until the very last minute. Because Beast meets Heart of Darkness would be great for an almost too big number of reasons, which easily range through all the themes of Beast and even more. Not to mention that would give us more NWoD's Africa, which would be awesome in its own right.<br /> <br /> I honestly hope the writers will consider this Era but, if it's not the one who gets picked, I'll probably read some books on the matter so I can write it myself, just to give you an idea how much I'm captivated by this idea. Not saying that my Dark Era would be on the same level of quality of one made by Beast writers (it just won't), but I'll have no problems whatsoever doing that if needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-19-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:58:29-07:00","id":561066,"title":"","content":"I really hope we go into the really old recesses of history, so as to feel appropriately mythical with your Hero narratives. Make your Begotten really feel like something out of Gilgamesh or the Odyssey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:16:13-07:00","id":561074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=546149#post546149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...and now, as someone who was kind of 'meh' about the Mage Neolithic Era and voted against it I am so glad we are getting it.<br /> If I had known it was going to be pre-Sundering I would not only have voted for it, but done a merry jig when it won. Seriously, I would have googled how to do a jig then practiced until I did a merry one!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think we can actually thank the backer who donated 5,000 extra words to the chapter requesting it be made a crossover setting with Werewolf. IIRC, Stew (the Werewolf developer) was offered the choice to make it Pre-Sundering or Post-Sundering but Pre-Oath-of-the-Moon, and he opted to explore the Pangean era.<br /> <br /> The implication I like about the Sundering being that (relatively speaking) recent, is that it was the agricultural revolution that weakened Father Wolf, the spirit of &quot;the hunt&quot; and &quot;predation&quot; itself - leading to his death at his own pack's fangs and claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T18:35:04-07:00","id":621774,"title":"","content":"Beast Dark Eras confirmed for Reconstruction South.<br /> <br /> I trust Matt enough to assume this will not be Dunning School b.s. about those evil Radicals oppressing the victimized Southern whites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-10-2015, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T21:25:27-07:00","id":621864,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm sort of wary. I'll wait until we actually hear about it to make judgements but I already wish they'd picked something different for Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T08:43:24-07:00","id":622286,"title":"","content":"The Reconstruction wouldn't have been my pick, but I'm honestly pretty happy that they chose it over the Civil War itself.<br /> <br /> All too often do the difficult, ambiguous times after the Civil War and the failures of its aftermath get brushed over in favor of the stories told during the conflict and assuming that victory had flawless results once obtained (and that the ideals <i>identified </i>withthe war were properly achieved).<br /> <br /> It's dangerous ground to tread so far as portraying goes, but I trust Onyx Path will do a good job of it or they wouldn't have gone out of their way to use the era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:08:37-07:00","id":622499,"title":"","content":"There were basically two successive conflicts. The North won the first (the Civil War). The South won the second (the insurrection against Reconstruction). History as usual was written by the victors - in this case the victors of said insurrection. Hence the half-century of the Dunning School dominating Civil War and Reconstruction historography. &quot;It wasn't about slavery for the Confederacy! It was about State's Rights!&quot; &quot;The evil Radical Republicans oppressed the ex-Confederates!&quot; The North historically went along with this because it served the cause of national (white) unity. It's only been since the Civil Rights movement that historians have seriously reexamined the history surrounding Reconstruction, and how its primary function (which it ended up failing at thanks to too many concessions to the ex-Confederates) was to assure the rights of freed slaves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T06:13:43-07:00","id":626539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=622286#post622286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Reconstruction wouldn't have been my pick, but I'm honestly pretty happy that they chose it over the Civil War itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, one of the writers on this Dark Era, Hayley Margules, is a historian. We talked about possibilities for the Era, and she actually helped me decide that the Reconstruction would be better than the War itself. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry too much that we're going to argue &quot;states' rights.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:15:52-07:00","id":626601,"title":"","content":"For a future Dark Era book, early 20th century America strikes me as very fertile ground for <i>Beast</i>. There's Prohibition, when mobsters and the FBI clashed over moonshining, and rum running. You've got the rise of the Klan, and the early days of the civil rights movement. And you've got all those wonderful labor conflicts (they got so bad, in Appalachia, they're remembered as the Mine Wars).<br /> <br /> It was an era when the law was . . . mutable, with tommy guns and cold hard cash defining &quot;justice&quot;. So many people carved out their personal fiefs, and cops had to be quick on the draw . . . or come home in body bags (assuming there were cops, period). It was an era when bad things walked openly, and there are simply so many opportunities to <i>FEED</i><br /> <br /> * Imagine Beasts with a hunger for Power embracing Morganization, acting as strikebreakers (or industrialists!) crushing workers in the interest of efficiency . . . And Beasts with appetites for Punishment and Ruin striking back through the unions. . .<br /> <br /> There are great accounts from the period, of dynamitings and arson by the unions, and of strikebreakers mutilating women and forcing strikers to flee through the woods . . .<br /> <br /> * And can't you just picture a bunch of Klan wannabes getting in over their head, when they decide to lynch that creepy old black woman . . .<br /> <br /> * Or Elliot Ness and the Untouchables raiding a speakeasy, or moonshine still, only to run afoul of the &quot;owner&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=626539#post626539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, one of the writers on this Dark Era, Hayley Margules, is a historian. We talked about possibilities for the Era, and she actually helped me decide that the Reconstruction would be better than the War itself.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry too much that we're going to argue &quot;states' rights.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You should at least touch on it, though. No one goes to war (knowingly) for an evil cause. And when the bullets start flying, <i>any</i> principle can be quickly forgotten. You're fighting for the man next to you, and desperately praying to God that you make it one more day. . .<br /> <br /> If you make it simply, &quot;North=good, South=bad&quot;, you risk stripping the Civil War of its brother-against-brother dynamic, which helped make it such a tragic event. And, given that this <i>is</i> the World of Darkness, the North probably had more than its fair share of demons (figuratively speaking), and dark motives . . .<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see what you do with Reconstruction, though. I'd have thought it'd be more of a Changeling era, what with the returning Confederates, newly freed slaves, and Northern carpetbaggers, all trying to navigate a world gone strange. And realizing that &quot;going home&quot; or reaching the promised land, is far easier said than done. . .<br /> <br /> Plus, can't you just see the James gang as a motley of changelings?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Two events you might want to look into, for the Reconstruction era, would be the rise of Alan Pinkerton (and his eponymous detective agency), out of Chicago. He (and his agents) were agents of law and order (and occasionally oppression) in an era before there was an FBI or state police.<br /> <br /> And the Hatfield-McCoy feud (in West Virginia and Kentucky) seems like fertile ground for Beasts, too. Two extended clans waging their own private war in a region where &quot;the law doesn't go&quot;, while a small army of bounty hunters and private detectives tried to bring the combatants to justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  typo 08-14-2015, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:54:17-07:00","id":626695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=626601#post626601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You should at least touch on it, though. No one goes to war (knowingly) for an evil cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right - the South didn't consider Slavery to be evil. They considered it a positive good. It was 100% the cause they were fighting for, and they believed it a moral cause to protect their God given rights. In several of the Articles of Secession they complained that the Northern States had exercised TOO MUCH STATE SOVEREIGNTY by stripping Southerners of their property rights (forbidding Southeners to keep slaves they wanted to bring with them to the North).<br /> <br /> I agree though that most common soldiers are just fighting for home and the guy next to them.<br /> <br /> You're right that the North aren't a bunch of unambiguous good guys - they have tons of their own racist baggage (the dream of a &quot;free&quot; West was also imagined as an &quot;all white&quot; West for most Free Soilers, for example) - but the primary overriding cause of the war was Southern defense of the institution of slavery driving them to secede. &quot;State's Rights&quot; was not in any way shape or form a cause in the minds of the Confederates, save in the sense that they wanted the states to have the power to maintain slavery, and secede as they felt was necessary to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-14-2015, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T09:01:04-07:00","id":626701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=626601#post626601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a future Dark Era book, early 20th century America strikes me as very fertile ground for <i>Beast</i>. There's Prohibition, when mobsters and the FBI clashed over moonshining, and rum running. You've got the rise of the Klan, and the early days of the civil rights movement. And you've got all those wonderful labor conflicts (they got so bad, in Appalachia, they're remembered as the Mine Wars).</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot begin to express how perfect a Jazz/Prohibition/Rise-of-the-Klan age 20s crossover era for Vampire and Beast!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:21:44-08:00","id":784180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/494739-beast-dark-eras?p=496194#post496194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a Beast/Innocents crossover in the Blitz would be nice. What if Peter Pan was actually a Beast and Neverland it's Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm late to this, and we obviously know what the era ended up being, but having wanted Innocents/Blitz more than literally anything proposed, when I was asked what I thought we could do for the Dark Era, y'all should know that I was immediately like &quot;IS THERE ANYWAY WE CAN DO THE BLITZ&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 12-11-2015, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}